  <div id="sutta">
  
    <h4 id="thig2.4" class="h1">Thig 2:4  Aḍḍhkāsī</h4>
          <div class="verse">
            <p>All of the Kāsi countryside:</p>
            <p>My fee was equal to that.</p>
            <p>Having made that my price,</p>
            <p>the town<span class="fn"><a href="#thig2.4note01">1</a></span><!--end fn cite--> set me as priceless in price.</p>
            <p>But then I became disenchanted with my body,</p>
            <p>and—disenchanted—dispassionate:</p>
            <p>“May I not run again &amp; again</p>
            <p>through birth &amp; the wandering-on.”</p>
            <p class="v2">The three knowledges</p>
            <p class="v4">have been realized.</p>
            <p class="v2">The Buddha’s bidding</p>
            <p class="v4">done.</p>
          </div><!--end verse-->
          <div class="note">
            <p class="notetitle">Note</p><!--end notetitle-->
            <p id="thig2.4note01">1. Reading <em>nigamo</em> with the Thai edition. The Burmese and Sinhalese editions read <em>negamo,</em> “the townspeople.”</p>
          </div><!--end notes-->
          <p class="seealso">See also: <a href="../../AN/AN7_48.html">AN 7:48</a></p><!--end seealso-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
